# Planning/report HTML files -- generated docs, not project source.
# Anchored to the repo ROOT on purpose: a bare "*.html" also swallowed
# frontend/index.html, which is Vite's entry point -- without it a fresh
# clone cannot run the demo frontend at all.
/*.html

# Ad-hoc visual sanity-check outputs
check_*.png

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Large, regeneratable data -- not committed to keep the repo small.
# CARLA-generated anomalies come from generate_anomalies.py; Cityscapes/
# Fishyscapes are external downloads (see config.py's path constants).
data/images/
data/masks/
# The 5 miscategorized/oversized CARLA props pulled out of the bank during
# curation (see PLAN.md). Same kind of data as data/images|masks, so it is
# ignored for the same reason -- kept on disk, not deleted, but not shipped.
data/_excluded_objects/
# COCO cutout bank (~190MB, 3000 objects) and the raw val2017 download
# (~1GB) behind it. Both are rebuilt from scratch by
# download_coco_anomalies.py, on the pod as well as locally.
data/coco_objects/
data/_coco_download/

# Trained checkpoints and experiment tracking -- large binaries, regenerated
# by train.py / logged fresh on every run
checkpoints/
mlruns/
# Same artifacts, but landing at the repo root instead of checkpoints/ --
# happens when scp-ing results off a RunPod pod with "." as the destination
# (see RUNPOD_GUIDE.md Step 9). Caught a 342MB checkpoint accidentally
# committed this way once already -- don't let it recur.
/*.pth
/mlflow.db
/train.log
/train_*.log

# Local zip archives created for RunPod upload (make_upload.py, see RUNPOD_GUIDE.md)
*.zip

# Claude Code's project memory -- machine/session-specific working notes,
# not project source. Keep it local, never push it.
CLAUDE.md

# Claude Code's local working state. .claude/worktrees/ in particular holds
# full checked-out copies of this repo (agent worktrees), including config
# files carrying this machine's absolute C:\Users\... dataset paths -- those
# must never reach a collaborator.
.claude/

# Ad-hoc stdout/stderr redirects from one-off debugging commands -- not
# meant to be kept around, let alone committed.
check_error*.txt
*_log.txt
prompt.txt

# Cached demo output regenerated by server.py at startup (see README's
# "Live demo" section) -- delete + restart the backend to rebuild.
static/generated/
demo_output/

# Frontend build artifacts / dependencies -- regenerated by npm install /
# npm run build, not source.
frontend/node_modules/
frontend/dist/
static_react/

# CARLA route recordings from record_route.py (RGB frames + masks + poses,
# hundreds of MB per route). Deterministic from --seed, so re-record rather
# than commit. Default output names are video_pilot / video_<name>.
/video_*/

# Rendered video / per-frame panel outputs, if written outside static/generated/
*.mp4

# Local environment / secrets, if any ever get created
.env
.env.local

# Transcript from run_video.ps1 (the eval numbers are kept in eval_video_town02.log)
/run_video.log

# explain.py outputs (per-image JSON + example strips); numbers are kept in explain_x1.log
/explain_out/

# 3-agent workflow state (reports, brief, exp_v2 snapshot, pre-edit copies). Local only:
# it holds machine paths and a copy of another branch.
/agent_state/

# Internal process notes (mistake log, frozen old plan). Local only, not project source.
/MISTAKES.md
/PLAN_HISTORY.md

# The demo video IS needed by a fresh clone (/demo plays it; ~16 MB, under GitHub's
# 100 MB limit). Everything else *.mp4 stays ignored.
!/static/video/twinguard_video_town02_pasted.mp4
